{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Rejoice, Zebulun.</b> He was dissatisfied with his portion, as our Sages taught: Zebulun risked his life to die, because Naphtali was on the heights of the field. Therefore Moses said to him: <b>rejoice, Zebulun</b>, in your portion, and do not be saddened that your portion fell on the sea, for you profit from it, as he proceeds to explain." "<b>When you go out.</b> Moses our teacher blessed each and every one with what he needed. He would go out in commerce, as it is written: 'Zebulun shall dwell by the shore of the seas.' Therefore he blessed him that he be guarded when he goes out." "<b>And Issachar in your tents.</b> His land was good for sowing, and he would sit in tents to guard his fields, and Moses prayed that he succeed and rejoice in his fields. And so Jacob said to him: 'resting between the saddlebags' — between the borders, to guard his fields."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:28.664060062Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}